                <pb facs="0024" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20 Missions/2–1148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-02-11T20:00:00+08:00">February 11, 1948—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 11—8:37 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>280. I understand that the United States has responsibilities other than those in
                    China and I shall be guided by your 212, February 9, <pb facs="0025" n="15"
                        xml:id="pg15"/> 8 p.m. In this connection, however, you may wish to see
                    latest plea from Wei for ammunition.…</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
